 {:name "prove-weak-L2-convergence-by-Vitali-on-products-over-infinite-measure"
  :lane :solve-lane
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Derive weak `L²` convergence on an infinite measure space from almost-everywhere convergence and a uniform `L²` bound."
   :route
   ["Fix an arbitrary test function `h ∈ L²` and reduce the weak-convergence goal to convergence of the integrals of the products `fₙh`."
    "Use Hölder to control the products in `L¹`."
    "Prove uniform integrability on small-measure sets from the uniform `L²` bound and the fixed test function."
    "Because the ambient measure is infinite, separately prove uniform tightness from the `L²` tail of `h`; small-set uniform integrability alone is not enough."
    "Combine the a.e. convergence of `fₙh` to `gh` with both controls and apply the infinite-measure Vitali theorem `tendsto_Lp_of_tendsto_ae` in `L¹`."
    "Translate the resulting `L¹` convergence into convergence of the pairings."]
   :key-api
   ["MeasureTheory.tendsto_Lp_of_tendsto_ae"
    "MeasureTheory.UniformIntegrable"
    "MeasureTheory.UniformIntegrableOn"
    "Hölder inequality"]
